    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-66832",
    ":question/problem": "Find the exact solution to the equation $3({4}^{y})-14=19.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({4}^{y})-14 & =19 \\\\ 3({4}^{y}) & =33 \\\\ {4}^{y} & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{4}$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{4}\u2061({4}^{y}) & ={log}_{4}\u2061(11) \\\\ y & ={log}_{4}\u2061(11)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y={log}_{4}\u2061(11).$"
  },
