    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-31891",
    ":question/problem": "Given that ${5}^{2a+3}-13=25,$ find the value of $a$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{2a+3}-13 & =25 \\\\ {5}^{2a+3} & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{5}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{2a+3} & =38 \\\\ {log}_{5}\u2061({5}^{2a+3}) & ={log}_{5}\u2061(38) \\\\ 2a+3 & ={log}_{5}\u2061(38)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3 & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(38)}{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(5)} \\\\ 2a & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(38)}{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(5)}-3 \\\\ a & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(38)}{2\\operatorname{log}\u2061(5)}-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\na\u2248-0.370\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."
  },
