    ":question/id": "e0b9a214-575e-56bc-9016-1d953bb568c0",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-100254",
    ":question/problem": "Given that ${7}^{5x}+8=34,$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{5x}+8 & =34 \\\\ {7}^{5x} & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{7}$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{5x} & =26 \\\\ {log}_{7}\u2061({7}^{5x}) & ={log}_{7}\u2061(26) \\\\ 5x & ={log}_{7}\u2061(26) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{5}{log}_{7}\u2061(26)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\u22480.335\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."
